We introduce a novel method for manipulating garments that combines visual recognition and manipulation strategies. Our key contribution is the concept of canonical alignment, which enables consistent garment manipulation by relating manipulation actions to their standard form. We demonstrate this through the Fabric Funnels framework, a multi-faceted garment manipulation model that includes tasks such as hole punching, filling, and insertion, as well as garment folding and sorting. The proposed method significantly outperforms existing state-of-the-art approaches to these manipulation tasks. Additional resources, including video and code, are available at https://summetropolis.com/fabric_funnels/. This research has been accepted for publication in ACM Transactions on Graphics and ACM Transactions on Graphics Special Issue. 

